50` (Map) requires investigation.\n\n\n**Exploring Network Redirection Alternatives**\n\nAdding the route `109.62.64.18/32` via `172.30.198.33` fails because the gateway must be within the local subnet; the correct gateway for the `/29` subnet is `172.30.198.54`. However, direct forwarding to `172.30.198.33` isn't possible, requiring a different approach.\n\nOne method is to use a forwarding utility like `socat`, or similar proxy/tunnel tools to listen on the loopback interface for connections to `109.62.64.18:9443` and forward them to `172.30.198.33:9443`. This involves assigning `109.62.64.18/32` to the loopback interface on the proxy host. This allows any local connection to `109.62.64.18:9443` to be redirected to the internal server.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"~/.ansible/kssh -u superuser 172.30.198.49 '\ngrep -rn \"109.62.64.18\" /etc/centreon* /etc/httpd/ /var/www/ 2>/dev/null || true\ngrep -rn \"map.extranetclient\" /etc/centreon* /etc/httpd/ /var/www/ 2>/dev/null || true\n'","Cwd":"/home/koby","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Check Centreon config on 172.30.198.49 for Map URL"}}]}
