{"step_index":370,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T12:22:24Z","content":"Here is the complete, consolidated configuration guide for both the **Reverse Proxy** and the **Backend Central** servers.\n\n---\n\n### Part 1: Reverse Proxy Configuration (`th2-revproxyp-fe1` — `172.30.198.33`)\n\n#### 1. Nginx Virtual Host Configuration\nEdit file: [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf)\n\nEnsure the port `9443` block is configured as follows:\n\n```nginx\n# HTTPS redirect MAP\nserver {\n    listen              9443 ssl http2 reuseport;\n    server_name         map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr 109.62.64.18;\n\n    # SSL (same certificate as port 443)\n    ssl_certificate     /etc/letsencrypt/live/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/fullchain.pem;\n    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/privkey.pem;\n\n    # Security headers\n    include             nginxconfig.io/security.conf;\n\n    # Dedicated logs for port 9443\n    access_log          /var/log/nginx/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr-9443-access.log;\n    error_log           /var/log/nginx/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr-9443-error.log warn;\n\n    # Explicit root redirection to Centreon Map web application\n    location = / {\n        return 301 /centreon-map/;\n    }\n\n    # Reverse proxy to Centreon Map (Tomcat HTTPS on port 9443)\n    location / {\n        proxy_pass                 https://172.30.198.50:9443;\n        proxy_ssl_verify           off;\n\n        include                    nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf;\n        proxy_set_header Host      $http_host;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Ssl   on;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port  9443;\n\n        proxy_redirect             http:// https://;\n        proxy_headers_hash_max_size    1024;\n        proxy_headers_hash_bucket_size 128;\n    }\n\n    # Additional standard rules (favicon, gzip, etc.)\n    include nginxconfig.io/general.conf;\n}\n```\n\n* Validate and reload Nginx:\n  ```bash\n  sudo nginx -t\n  sudo systemctl reload nginx\n  ```\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Loopback IP Persistence (Across Server Reboots)\nTo ensure the reverse proxy continues accepting traffic destined for `109.62.64.18` after a reboot:\n\nCreate file: `/etc/network/interfaces.d/lo-alias`\n```text\nauto lo:1\niface lo:1 inet static\n    address 109.62.64.18/32\n```\nApply it immediately without rebooting:\n```bash\nsudo ip addr add 109.62.64.18/32 dev lo\n```\n\n---\n\n### Part 2: Backend Server Configuration (`th2-centprop-be1` — `172.30.198.49`)\n\n#### 1. Internal Host Resolution\nAdd this entry to [`/etc/hosts`](file:///etc/hosts) on `th2-centprop-be1`:\n\n```text\n172.30.198.33 map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n```\n\n* **Why**: This directs all internal backend requests and the UI's `[Test connection to server]` checks straight to the reverse proxy over the LAN, completely bypassing the firewall's hairpin NAT limitation.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Centreon Web UI Settings\n1. Log in to Centreon Web: **`https://extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/`**\n2. Navigate to: **Administration $\\rightarrow$ Extensions $\\rightarrow$ Options**\n3. Under the **| Centreon MAP settings** section, configure:\n\n| Field | Value | Purpose |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`MAP Engine server address`** | `https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443` | URL given to the **external user's browser** to load Map views and WebSockets |\n| **`MAP server address as seen by Central`** | `https://th2-centprop-map1.prod.intranet` | Direct internal LAN address used by **Central** for backend-to-backend synchronization |\n| **`MAP Engine server`** | `Yes` | Enables the HTML5 web map engine |\n\n4. Click the blue **[Test connection to server]** button next to *MAP Engine server address*:\n   * It will immediately return <span style=\"color:green\">**SUCCESS**</span>.\n5. Click **Save** at the bottom of the page.\n\n---\n\n### Part 3: Verification Commands\n\n#### 1. Verify from Backend Central (`172.30.198.49`):\n```bash\ncurl -k -i -L https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443/\n```\n* **Expected Result**: Receives <span style=\"color:yellow\">**HTTP/2 301**</span> (redirect to `/centreon-map/`), followed by <span style=\"color:green\">**HTTP/2 401 Unauthorized**</span> from the Centreon Map API.\n\n#### 2. Verify from External Internet:\n```bash\ncurl -k -i -L https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443/\n```\n* **Traffic Path**: Client Browser $\\rightarrow$ Public DNS (`109.62.64.18:9443`) $\\rightarrow$ Firewall DNAT $\\rightarrow$ Reverse Proxy (`172.30.198.33:9443`) $\\rightarrow$ Centreon Map (`172.30.198.50:9443`).","thinking":"**Documenting IP Address Persistence**\n\nInvestigating configuration files shows that the specified directory holds network interface definitions on one server. Determined that modifying the loopback interface's configuration or using an `ip addr` command within a defined structure ensures the specific IP address remains active after reboots. This is the persistent configuration method needed.\n\n\n"}
