{"step_index":437,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T12:52:27Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. It should be noted that 109.62.64.18:9443 redirects to Map [172.30.198.50].\n2. [root@th2-centprop-be1 ~]# ip route show\ndefault via 172.30.198.54 dev ens192 proto static metric 100 \n172.30.198.48/29 dev ens192 proto kernel scope link src 172.30.198.49 metric 100 \n[root@th2-centprop-be1 ~]# ip route add 109.62.64.18/32 via 172.30.198.33\nError: Nexthop has invalid gateway.\n3. The external user connects to the url extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr on 443 which is the Centreon Web UI. Then he connects to the Map server using the Map option [/home/koby/Pictures/Screenshots/Screenshot From 2026-09-10 15-56-25.png].\n4. Give all the configurations that need to done on the backend and reverse proxy!\n5. Please check the nginx config on the reverse proxy and modify it if required.\n6. I also added lo-alias interface!\n7. [root@th2-centprop-be1 ~]# cat /etc/hosts\n127.0.0.1   localhost localhost.localdomain localhost4 localhost4.localdomain4\n::1         localhost localhost.localdomain localhost6 localhost6.localdomain6\n#127.0.1.1   th2-centprop-be1.infra.intranet.local  th2-centprop-be1\n172.30.198.49    th2-centprop-be1.infra.intranet.local    th2-centprop-be1\n172.30.198.57    th2-centprop-db1.infra.intranet.local    th2-centprop-db1\n172.30.166.49   mau-centprop-pol1.infra.intranet.local  mau-centprop-pol1\n172.30.38.49    mtq-centprop-pol1.infra.intranet.local  mtq-centprop-pol1\n#127.0.0.1 extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n#172.30.198.33 extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n172.30.198.33 map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n8. I did the test but failed. /home/koby/Pictures/Screenshots/Screenshot From 2026-09-10 16-39-40.png\n/home/koby/Pictures/Screenshots/Screenshot From 2026-09-10 16-40-10.png\n9. Please stop here\n10. Provide me the findings, Configurations applied (Explain why) and current status of the chain.\n\n<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n* **Objective**: Establish and verify the redirection and reverse proxy chain for Centreon Map on port `9443`, enabling external users connecting to Centreon Web (`extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:443`) to seamlessly access the Centreon Map UI (`172.30.198.50`).\n* **Environment**:\n  * **Reverse Proxy**: `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33:30`, Debian, Nginx 1.18.0 + ModSecurity).\n  * **Centreon Central Backend**: `th2-centprop-be1` (`172.30.198.49:30`, AlmaLinux 8.6).\n  * **Centreon Map Server**: `172.30.198.50:9443` (Tomcat HTTPS).\n  * **Public VIP & DNS**: `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` $\\rightarrow$ `109.62.64.18`.\n  * **Firewall Gateway**: `172.30.198.54`.\n* **Resolved Ambiguities**:\n  * Rectified public IP typo: `109.62.64.18` (confirmed on authoritative DNS `th2-dnsp-mst1`), not `109.62.62.18`.\n  * Clarified role of Centreon Web settings: `MAP Engine server address` is delivered to client browsers, while `MAP server address as seen by Central` is used for internal backend-to-backend communication.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress & Configurations Applied\n\n#### A. Created Nginx Master Agent (`koby-bowser-nginx`)\n* Declared in [`~/.claude/agents/koby-bowser-nginx.md`](file:///home/koby/.claude/agents/koby-bowser-nginx.md).\n* Registered globally in [`~/.gemini/config/skills/koby-bowser-nginx/SKILL.md`](file:///home/koby/.gemini/config/skills/koby-bowser-nginx/SKILL.md).\n* Registered in the active Antigravity session via `define_subagent`.\n\n#### B. Reverse Proxy Configuration (`th2-revproxyp-fe1` — `172.30.198.33`)\n1. **Virtual Host**: [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf):\n   * **Port 443 (Centreon Web)**:\n     * Preserved proxy to `http://172.30.198.49` with `/` $\\rightarrow$ `/centreon/` redirect and `/lorawan/data` ingest on port 8443.\n   * **Port 9443 (Centreon Map)**:\n     * `listen 9443 ssl http2 reuseport;`\n     * `server_name map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr 109.62.64.18;`\n     * **Redirection**: Added `location = / { return 301 /centreon-map/; }` to eliminate Tomcat root 404 errors.\n     * **Proxy target**: Fixed `proxy_pass https://172.30.198.50:9443;` with `proxy_ssl_verify off;` (resolves initial 502 Bad Gateway).\n     * **Header preservation**: Configured `proxy_set_header Host $http_host;`, `proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;`, `proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port 9443;` so Tomcat maintains port `:9443` on internal redirects.\n2. **Loopback Alias Persistence**:\n   * Created [`/etc/network/interfaces.d/lo-alias`](file:///etc/network/interfaces.d/lo-alias):\n     ```text\n     auto lo:1\n     iface lo:1 inet static\n         address 109.62.64.18/32\n     ```\n   * Applied live via `ip addr add 109.62.64.18/32 dev lo` (verified with `ifup --no-act lo:1`).\n\n#### C. Backend Central Configuration (`th2-centprop-be1` — `172.30.198.49`)\n* Added entry to [`/etc/hosts`](file:///etc/hosts):\n  ```text\n  172.30.198.33 map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n  ```\n  * **Why**: Bypasses the lack of Hairpin NAT on the firewall gateway, allowing Central to resolve and route directly to the Reverse Proxy over the internal network.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n\n1. **Root Cause of Initial 502 Bad Gateway on Port 9443**:\n   * Nginx previously targeted `proxy_pass http://172.30.198.50;` (plain HTTP port 80). Port 80 on `.50` was closed (`Connection refused`). Centreon Map (Apache Tomcat) actually listens on port `9443` with TLS (`https`).\n2. **Firewall Hairpin NAT Barrier**:\n   * Synchronized packet capture (`tcpdump` on `172.30.198.33`) while `172.30.198.49` requested `109.62.64.18:9443` captured **`0 packets`**.\n   * The firewall (`172.30.198.54`) only applies the DNAT rule to incoming WAN traffic and drops internal LAN/DMZ requests to its own VIP.\n3. **Subnet Isolation Between `.49` and `.33`**:\n   * Backend `.49` is in `172.30.198.48/29` (gw `.54`), while reverse proxy `.33` is in `172.30.198.32/29`.\n   * Direct `ip route add ... via 172.30.198.33` returned `Error: Nexthop has invalid gateway` because gateways must be on the local `/29` link.\n   * Kernel module insertion (`nft_nat`) is locked down on AlmaLinux 8 (`Operation not permitted`).\n   * `/etc/hosts` mapping to `172.30.198.33` proved to be the most reliable, non-intrusive solution for internal resolution.\n4. **Why the UI \"Test connection to